{
  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) leads at 0.725 acc, with all four components individually validated as the best choices (scvi_n200 >> pca/scgpt; imagenet_vit_l > resnet50; transformer > avgpool; weighted ≥ concat). No remaining untested config combines all four best components, so beating 0.725 is unlikely. This experiment tests the closest untested variant—swapping imagenet_vit_l→resnet50 and weighted→concat while keeping the top RNA encoder and transformer aggregation—clarifying whether a cheaper image backbone with concat fusion can approach the best accuracy. It is the most informative remaining test because it isolates the combined effect of the two 'second-best' choices, directly informing the cost-accuracy tradeoff. Expected relative cost: moderate, roughly 4–6 GPU hours (resnet50+transformer previously cost 6.22 in config_015; concat fusion adds little overhead), which is comparable to or slightly below the imagenet_vit_l transformer runs."
}

